# GitHub issue labels

When creating or editing issues on **The-Allsparks/ftc-dev-tools**, follow [docs/issue-labels.md](../../docs/issue-labels.md).

## Quick rules

- Add **one** of `priority: P0`, `priority: P1`, `priority: P2` to every roadmap issue.
- Add **at least one surface**: `shared-core`, `vscode`, `cli`, `mcp`, or `vision` (or `documentation` / `architecture` for docs/design-only work).
- Epics: include `epic`.
- Vision work: include `vision` plus the relevant sub-label (`limelight`, `webview`, etc.).

## Catalog

Canonical label sets per issue title: `scripts/issue-label-catalog.json`.

After adding or retitling an issue:

1. Update the catalog with the full label list (mirror similarly titled issues from #48+).
2. Run `npm run check:issue-labels` or `node scripts/issue-labels.mjs apply --dry-run`.

Do not invent new label names without adding them to `.github/labels.yml` first.
